# Cloudflare Pages response headers for orangeway.app
#
# THIS FILE IS THE SAFE BASELINE. The policy below is Report-Only, and that is
# what every environment gets unless something deliberately upgrades it.
# `scripts/csp-mode-plugin.ts` is that something: on a Cloudflare Pages build it
# reads CF_PAGES_BRANCH and rewrites this header to the enforcing
# `Content-Security-Policy` for branches listed in ENFORCING_BRANCHES (`dev`
# today, so orangeway.dev enforces and orangeway.app reports). It can only
# upgrade, never downgrade, so if the plugin is removed or never runs, every
# environment reports instead of blocking.
#
# Do not restore an enforcing header here. A static enforcing line applies to
# every environment at once, which is exactly the defect this replaced: the file
# used to claim prod stayed Report-Only while dev enforced, and nothing in the
# repository made that true. It was true only for as long as prod had not
# received the commit yet, which is a delay, not a gate.
#
# report-uri is deliberately kept: an enforcing policy still reports, and those
# reports are how a real break is caught. frame-ancestors and report-uri can
# only be delivered as a header, never via <meta>.
#
# Promotion criterion for adding `prod` to ENFORCING_BRANCHES: dev has run 48
# hours clean under enforcement AND QA has passed vault unlock, Turnstile and
# the support widget. Violations naming an EMPTY source are not attributable to
# any host and cannot be allow-listed, so they do not count against it; a
# violation naming a source we own or depend on does.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://support.orangeway.app https://eu-assets.i.posthog.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://eu.i.posthog.com https://pulse.orangeway.app https://support.orangeway.app; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://eu.i.posthog.com https://eu-assets.i.posthog.com https://pulse.orangeway.app https://support.orangeway.app wss://support.orangeway.app; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://support.orangeway.app; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; report-uri https://pulse.orangeway.app/api/1/security/?sentry_key=557469b0d58a45a3b7626e1329b014ee
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  # Force HTTPS for two years incl. subdomains; 'preload' opts into the browser
  # preload list. Orange Way is HTTPS-only behind Cloudflare, so this is safe.
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  # Deny powerful browser features the app never uses (defense in depth).
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
